# Build context for infra/railway/Dockerfile.api is the REPOSITORY ROOT.
#
# Without this file, `COPY apps/api/ ./` drags a host-built virtualenv into the image.
# This repo is developed on Windows, so apps/api/.venv contains Windows paths and a
# Scripts/ layout; landing it in a Linux image on top of the /opt/venv built in the
# builder stage corrupts interpreter resolution in ways that fail at runtime, not at
# build time. Everything below is either host-specific, secret, or reproducible.

# --- Python host artefacts -------------------------------------------------
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# --- JavaScript (the API image needs none of it) ---------------------------
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
apps/web
packages

# --- Secrets: never in an image layer --------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Version control and CI ------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# --- Local object storage: demo document bytes, not application code -------
storage/*
!storage/.gitkeep

# --- Editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode
.idea
.claude
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- Docs and tooling that do not belong in a runtime image ----------------
docs
evals
vercel.json
railway.json
Makefile
make.ps1
README.md
BUILD_BIBLE.md
ROADMAP.md
CLAUDE.md
PROMPT_W1_foundation.md
